  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Rights-Based Solutions for Vulnerable Migrants Through a Migrant Resource and Response Mechanism (MRRM) in the South of Libya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The risky and complex journeys undertaken by migrants, reaching Libya and beyond, expose them as well as host communities to multiple health risks. Due to the continuous and prolonged instability the health system is fragmented, ineffective and lacks the ability to respond to health needs of migrants and the Libyan population. The objective of this project is to contribute to advancing rights-based solutions to address the needs of vulnerable migrants in Libya through the migrant resource and response mechanism. IOM continues its critical interventions to directly support migrants, including to persons who have experienced distress, multiple displacement or challenges in accessing essential services. Migrants living in urban areas in and around Ghat as well as vulnerable cases from host communities are benefitting from a comprehensive approach that brings together a wide range of services and needs based assistance in one mechanism. Beneficiaries are receiving primary health care services, non-food items and hygiene kits, protection services and referral to various more specialized types of assistance. Simultaneously, IOM is disseminating information materials about the risks of irregular migration and is working towards increased acceptance of migrants by the local community through the implementation of a community cohesion initiative.</narrative>
  </description>
